  "title": "11: Conics",
  "originalText": "In this chapter, you will learn about conics, including circles, parabolas, ellipses, and hyperbolas. Then you will use what you learn to investigate systems of nonlinear equations.\n\n11.1: Prelude to Conics\n\n11.2: Distance and Midpoint Formulas and Circles\n\n11.2E: Exercises\n\n11.3: Parabolas\n\n11.3E: Exercises\n\n11.4: Ellipses\n\n11.4E: Exercises\n\n11.5: Hyperbolas\n\n11.5E: Exercises\n\n11.6: Solving Systems of Nonlinear Equations\n\n11.6E: Exercises\n\nChapter 11 Review Exercises\n\nThis page titled 11: Conics was last modified on Mon, 14 Feb 2022 01:05:18 GMT and is shared under a CC BY  4.0  license and was authored, remixed, and/or curated by OpenStax via source content that was edited to the style and standards of the LibreTexts platform.",
